<title>DENMARK: Danish August North Sea oil production up 3.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish August North Sea oil production up 3.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) oil production from its North Sea fields rose 3.1 percent in August from July, operator A.P. Moeller Group said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A spokesman said production was 910,000 tonnes in August or 214,845 barrels per day (bpd), compared with 208,337 bpd in July.</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields.</p>
<p>Production data (in thousand bpd):  </p>
<p> Field			Aug 96	 July 96	 Aug 95</p>
<p> Dan			   69.7	    68.6	    58.4</p>
<p> Kraka			  4.9	     5.9	     7.3</p>
<p> Regnar			 0.8	     1.0	     1.3</p>
<p> Gorm			  52.0	    54.5	    48.5</p>
<p> Skjold			30.6	    32.9	    40.3</p>
<p> Rolf			   4.1	     3.7	     4.0</p>
<p> Dagmar			 0.4	     0.5	     0.6</p>
<p> Tyra			  19.7	    19.4	    21.6</p>
<p> Valdemar		     3.0	     1.4	     2.3</p>
<p> Roar			   5.8	     4.8		-</p>
<p> Svend			  23.8	   15.6		-</p>
<p> Total			 214.8	  208.3	   184.2</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc own 46 percent and 15 percent respectively. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom, +45-33-96950</p>
</text>
